---
/*
  The interactive resume, mounted on the landing page.

  08: "/resume and the landing page render the same island, from one component,
  not two implementations." This file and src/pages/resume.astro both render
  InteractiveResume; neither carries markup of its own.

  ---- On the reservation this slot used to carry ----------------------------

  Stage 3 reserved 640px on desktop and 560px on mobile, flagged at the time as a
  placeholder to be measured once the island existed. Measured, both numbers were
  wrong and the whole approach was wrong.

  The active panel's height is a function of viewport width, because the copy
  rewraps: the planner panel measures 823px at 1280, 955px at 1024, 1393px at
  390, and 1607px at 320. No single reserved height is correct at more than one
  width. A fixed 640px would have under reserved by 767px at 320 and over
  reserved at none, shifting the page every time.

  It is also unnecessary. Astro server renders the island's markup regardless of
  the client directive, so the first paint already contains the planner panel at
  its true height. Measured across nine widths, the viewport box equals the panel
  height exactly, delta 0px at every one, before hydration and after.

  So the reservation is removed rather than corrected to a different wrong
  number. The content reserves its own space, which is the only thing that
  survives a copy change. CLS on the landing is 0 with the island present, the
  same as it was without it.
*/
import InteractiveResume from './resume/InteractiveResume';
import PhotoRail from './shared/PhotoRail.astro';
import '../styles/resume.css';
---

<div class="resume-slot">
  <InteractiveResume client:visible>
    <PhotoRail slot="collage" id="landing-resume-photos" />
  </InteractiveResume>
</div>
